I agree, tourists are much easier to start
than many other classes, especially those with no
starting food.  I'd go with the daggers
instead of the short swords, though:
they may be a bit crappier in hand-to-hand
fighting early on, but once you advance them
and find an elven dagger or two they do OK.
More importantly, once you get them to Skilled
or Expert and gather a stack of 10 or so for
throwing from gnomes and dwarves in the mines,
you can kill most things before they can touch you.
Once my tourists start throwing daggers effectively,
the camera usually becomes a rarely-used backup.

And a stack of elven daggers at Expert, which can
usually be gathered and enchanted before you get
too far, will stay useful all the way through the game.
All that practice with the short sword will be useless
once you find a saber or a decent artifact.



